    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157">

                <pb facs="0411" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg401"/>

                <head>Her Majesty’s Foreign Office to Laird Brothers.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 4, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen:</hi> Earl Russell has been led to
                    understand that you have intimated that, while you were not in a position to
                    volunteer information respecting the iron-clad vessels lately launched and now
                    being fitted out at your yard, you would readily furnish information upon an
                    official application in writing being made to you for it.</p>
                <p>Under these circumstances, Lord Russell has instructed me to request you to
                    inform him, with as little delay as possible, on whose account, and with what
                    destination, these vessels have been built.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. H. LAYARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laird</hi> &amp; Co., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Birkenhead.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
